[[War on Valentines]]
|money drop = 2¢ - 8¢
}}

==Enemy==
This enemy dies once after attacking, similar to [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]], however has a 100% chance to [[Slow|slow]] cats for 10 seconds and a 100% chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] cats along with an [[Omni Strike]] attack that can reach up to 125 maximum range. It has almost a million health and immunities to most debuffs, meaning it will almost always be able to attack your cats, causing them to be applied with deadly effects.

==Strategy==
Don't bother trying to kill this enemy. Instead, bait his attacks with something along the lines of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] so he doesn't hit your important units. Alternatively, you can use slow and knockback immune units to ignore its effect on the battlefield completely, or you can use units who only resist/are immune to slow and take advantage of Wafer Cat XL's knockback to ensure their safety.

